---
const proofItems = [
  {
    title: 'Stronger homepage positioning',
    desc: 'Replace vague messaging with clearer buyer-facing language that improves first-impression trust.'
  },
  {
    title: 'Better service-page architecture',
    desc: 'Move from short brochure pages to pages that handle objections, clarify value, and support action.'
  },
  {
    title: 'Improved CTA flow',
    desc: 'Make the next step more obvious, more relevant, and easier to take across the site.'
  },
  {
    title: 'Cleaner SEO foundation',
    desc: 'Support better crawlability, internal linking, schema usage, and local intent alignment from launch.'
  },
];
---

<section class="section-padding bg-white">
  <div class="content-width">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[.95fr_1.05fr] gap-12 items-center mb-14">
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg mb-5">What We Mean by "Results"</h2>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-lg mb-6">
          We do not use fake screenshots, inflated ranking claims, or invented conversion numbers. When formal case studies are limited, we focus on proof that still matters: better structure, sharper positioning, cleaner internal logic, stronger conversion paths, and a site that looks and feels more credible to the right buyer.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-lg">
          In other words, the work should look more intentional, read more clearly, and make the business feel stronger before anyone ever gets on a call.
        </p>
      </div>

      <img
        src="/images/results-preview.webp"
        alt="Structured website improvement preview showing messaging, SEO, and conversion upgrades"
        class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 shadow-md object-cover aspect-[3/2]"
        width="900"
        height="600"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
      {proofItems.map((item) => (
        <div class="card-premium p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">{item.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-12">
      <a href="/results" class="btn-secondary">See Results & Approach</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
